 ## Background
-Segment Tracing was introduced by Galin et al. in 2020 [S1]. It was developed to address the limitations of Sphere Tracing, which uses a global Lipschitz bound that limits efficiency. The method leverages the structure of hierarchical skeletal implicit surfaces, where primitives are defined as a composition of a distance function and a kernel function, allowing for the computation of local directional Lipschitz bounds [S2]. It has been used in the context of ray tracing compactly supported primitives combined in a Blobtree [S2].
